    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d195">

                <pb facs="0445" n="413" xml:id="pg413"/>

                <head>195. Telegram From the Department of State to the Embassy in the Republic of
                        China<anchor n="0" xml:id="d195-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1958-10-20T13:40:00-04:00">October 20, 1958,
                            1:40 p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>369. Your 633.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d195-f2"/> On October 6 Department questioned
                    CNO’s office on advisability and necessity using LSD during cease-fire
                        period.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d195-f3"/> Department informed LSD essential in
                    delivering small landing craft needed in resupply especially of Tan islands.
                    Department was assured that LSD would proceed without US escort to point about
                    15 miles offshore whence landing craft would swim ashore. LSD also to be used
                    for landing craft pickup.</p>
                <p>In view subsequent US convoy escort suspension announcement October 8,<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d195-f4"/> would appreciate full explanation relating your
                    comment on item one reftel.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d195-f5"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Herter</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d195-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d195-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 793.00/10–2058. Secret; Niact; Limit
                    Distribution; No Distribution Outside Department. Drafted by Green, cleared by
                    Parsons and Martin, and approved by Herter.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d195-f2" n="1" xml:id="d195-f2-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d194-f2">footnote 1, Document 194</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d195-f3" n="2" xml:id="d195-f3-content">
                <p>The conversation was recorded in a memorandum of October 7 from Green to Parsons.
                    (Department of State, FE Files: Lot 63 D 76, Memoranda)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d195-f4" n="3" xml:id="d195-f4-content">
                <p>Cited in <ref target="#d165-f3">footnote 2, Document 165</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d195-f5" n="4" xml:id="d195-f5-content">
                <p>Drumright replied in telegram 642 from Taipei, October 21. (Department of State,
                    Central Files, 790.5411/10–2158; see Supplement)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
